# Creative Practice Ladder — {{TITLE}}

Each level requires preserved work and a short self-critique. Difficulty advances through one deliberate constraint at a time.

| Level | Purpose | Typical constraint | Gate evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| C0 | Baseline | Create from current ability without a tutorial | Untouched work plus intent and actual time |
| C1 | Isolated fundamental | Practice one element repeatedly | Variations plus comparison |
| C2 | Guided study | Reproduce or analyze an authorized reference | Reference citation plus divergence notes |
| C3 | Deliberate variation | Change one meaningful constraint | Prediction and before/after comparison |
| C4 | Independent piece | Work from a self-written brief | Final piece plus process evidence |
| C5 | Portfolio standard | Revise from critique for an audience | Accepted rubric evidence and reflection |

Reproduction is for study only unless rights and attribution allow publication. Never present copied work as original portfolio work.
